IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sfa-core`
IMPORT `sfa-periods`

-- Securities and Futures Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation (a rendering, not the official text).
-- Part 12, Division 4 (ss 232 to 236): civil penalty and civil liability. Layer 1: the law, objectively.
-- Amounts are Singapore dollars. Dates are Date day month year; periods are counted by sfa-periods (convention P1: the day of the event is not counted).
-- Powers of the Authority and of the court are encoded for what they mean to the person (what may be done to them, by when, up to how much).
-- GRANT-GROUP marks the groups Guide section 5 (ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 3) asks the fork register to list: [IF-NOTHING] a "may" whose "if" gate fails answers NOTHING (limit 1),
-- [WHERE-LISTED] a "may" gated by "where", "when" or "whenever" left as the Guide's periods ruling gives it (JUST FALSE), [ENTITLED] an "entitled" or "liable" claim.
-- SPLIT-SITE (ii) marks a "may" gated by "where", "whenever", "with the consent of", "after" or "who" and the like; SPLIT-SITE (i) an unmet element of a liability.

§ `s 232: civil penalty`

-- src:35866 | 232.—(1) Whenever it appears to the Authority that any person has
-- src:35867 | contravened any provision in this Part, the Authority may, with the
-- src:35868 | consent of the Public Prosecutor, bring an action in a court against the
-- src:35869 | person to seek an order for a civil penalty in respect of that
-- src:35870 | contravention.
@ref s 232(1) (src:35866-35870)
GIVEN
    `it appears to the Authority that the person has contravened a provision of Part 12` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the Authority that the person has contravened a provision of Part 12 of the Securities and Futures Act 2001?
    `the Public Prosecutor has consented to the action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Public Prosecutor consented to the Authority bringing the action?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 232(1) the Authority may bring an action in a court against the person to seek an order for a civil penalty` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `it appears to the Authority that the person has contravened a provision of Part 12`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Whenever it appears to the Authority that any person has contravened any provision in this Part" -- SPLIT-SITE (ii) [WHENEVER] -- GRANT-GROUP [WHERE-LISTED]
        IF NOT `the Public Prosecutor has consented to the action`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the Authority may, with the consent of the Public Prosecutor, bring an action" -- SPLIT-SITE (ii) [CONSENT] -- MARGINAL-READING (b)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:35872 | (2) If the court is satisfied on a balance of probabilities that the
-- src:35873 | person has contravened a provision in this Part, the court may make
-- src:35874 | an order against the person for the payment of a civil penalty of a sum
-- src:35875 | not exceeding the greater of the following:
@ref s 232(2) (src:35872-35875)
GIVEN
    `the court is satisfied on a balance of probabilities that the person has contravened a provision of Part 12` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied on a balance of probabilities that the person has contravened a provision of Part 12 of the Securities and Futures Act 2001?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 232(2) the court may make an order against the person for the payment of a civil penalty` MEANS
    IF `the court is satisfied on a balance of probabilities that the person has contravened a provision of Part 12`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the court may make an order against the person for the payment of a civil penalty" -- SPLIT-SITE (ii) [IF] -- MARGINAL-READING (a) -- GRANT-GROUP [IF-NOTHING]

@ref s 232(2) (src:35872-35875)
GIVEN
    `three times the profit gained or the loss avoided (the answer under section 232(2)(a))` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount in section 232(2)(a): 3 times the profit the person gained, or the loss the person avoided, as a result of the contravention?
    `the fixed amount (the answer under section 232(2)(b))` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount in section 232(2)(b): $2 million?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 232(2) the highest civil penalty the court may order` MEANS
    IF `three times the profit gained or the loss avoided (the answer under section 232(2)(a))` GREATER THAN `the fixed amount (the answer under section 232(2)(b))`
    THEN `three times the profit gained or the loss avoided (the answer under section 232(2)(a))`
    ELSE `the fixed amount (the answer under section 232(2)(b))`  -- "not exceeding the greater of the following"

-- src:35877 | (a) 3 times —
-- src:35879 | (i) the amount of the profit that the person gained as a
-- src:35880 | result of the contravention; or
-- src:35882 | (ii) the amount of the loss that the person avoided as a
-- src:35883 | result of the contravention;
@ref s 232(2)(a) (src:35877-35883)
GIVEN
    `the amount of the profit that the person gained as a result of the contravention` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the profit that the person gained as a result of the contravention? (0 if none)
    `the amount of the loss that the person avoided as a result of the contravention` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the loss that the person avoided as a result of the contravention? (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 232(2)(a) three times the profit gained or the loss avoided` MEANS
    IF `the amount of the profit that the person gained as a result of the contravention` GREATER THAN `the amount of the loss that the person avoided as a result of the contravention`
    THEN 3 TIMES `the amount of the profit that the person gained as a result of the contravention`
    ELSE 3 TIMES `the amount of the loss that the person avoided as a result of the contravention`  -- FORK F-232-2a: "or" read as the greater of the two when both are present

-- src:35885 | (b) $2 million.
@ref s 232(2)(b) (src:35885-35885)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 232(2)(b) the fixed amount in the cap` MEANS 2000000

-- src:35889 | (3) The civil penalty ordered under subsection (2) must not be less
-- src:35890 | than —
-- src:35895 | (a) in the case where the person is a corporation, $100,000;
-- src:35896 | and
-- src:35898 | (b) in any other case, $50,000.
@ref s 232(3) (src:35889-35898)
GIVEN
    `the person is a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a corporation (as section 2(1) defines "corporation")?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 232(3) the lowest civil penalty the court may order` MEANS
    IF `the person is a corporation`
    THEN 100000
    ELSE 50000  -- "in any other case"

@ref s 232(3) (src:35889-35898)
GIVEN
    `the civil penalty ordered` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the civil penalty ordered?
    `the highest civil penalty the court may order (the answer under section 232(2))` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the answer under section 232(2) for this person: the highest civil penalty the court may order?
    `the lowest civil penalty the court may order (the answer under section 232(3))` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the answer under section 232(3) for this person: the lowest civil penalty the court may order?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 232(2) and (3) the civil penalty ordered is within the limits` MEANS
    IF `the civil penalty ordered` AT MOST `the highest civil penalty the court may order (the answer under section 232(2))` AND `the civil penalty ordered` AT LEAST `the lowest civil penalty the court may order (the answer under section 232(3))`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "not exceeding the greater of the following" "must not be less than"

-- src:35902 | (4) Despite subsections (2) and (3), the court may make an order
-- src:35903 | against a person against whom an action has been brought under this
-- src:35904 | section if the Authority, with the consent of the Public Prosecutor, has
-- src:35905 | agreed to allow the person to consent to the order with or without
-- src:35906 | admission of a contravention of a provision in this Part and the order
-- src:35907 | may be made on such terms as may be agreed between the Authority
-- src:35908 | and the defendant.
@ref s 232(4) (src:35902-35908)
GIVEN
    `the action has been brought against the person under section 232` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an action been brought against the person under section 232?
    `the Authority, with the consent of the Public Prosecutor, has agreed to allow the person to consent to the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority, with the consent of the Public Prosecutor, agreed to allow the person to consent to the order, with or without admission of a contravention?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 232(4) the court may make the order on the terms agreed between the Authority and the defendant despite subsections (2) and (3)` MEANS
    IF `the action has been brought against the person under section 232` AND `the Authority, with the consent of the Public Prosecutor, has agreed to allow the person to consent to the order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the court may make an order against a person against whom an action has been brought under this section if the Authority, with the consent of the Public Prosecutor, has agreed" -- SPLIT-SITE (ii) [IF] -- MARGINAL-READING (a) -- GRANT-GROUP [IF-NOTHING]

-- src:35910 | (5) Nothing in this section prevents the Authority from entering
-- src:35911 | into an agreement with any person to pay, with or without admission
-- src:35912 | of liability, a civil penalty within the limits referred to in
-- src:35913 | subsection (2) or (3) for a contravention of any provision in this Part.
@ref s 232(5) (src:35910-35913)
GIVEN
    `the agreement is between the Authority and the person to pay a civil penalty, with or without admission of liability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the agreement one between the Authority and the person to pay a civil penalty for a contravention of a provision of Part 12, with or without admission of liability?
    `the civil penalty agreed is within the limits referred to in subsection (2) or (3) (the answer under section 232(2) and (3))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question "the civil penalty is within the limits" answer for the agreed amount? (JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 232(5) section 232 does not prevent the Authority from entering into the agreement` MEANS
    IF `the agreement is between the Authority and the person to pay a civil penalty, with or without admission of liability` AND (`the civil penalty agreed is within the limits referred to in subsection (2) or (3) (the answer under section 232(2) and (3))` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a civil penalty within the limits referred to in subsection (2) or (3)"

-- src:35915 | (6) A civil penalty imposed under this section must be paid into the
-- src:35916 | Consolidated Fund and is to be treated as a judgment debt due to the
-- src:35917 | Government for the purposes of section 10 of the Government
-- src:35918 | Proceedings Act 1956.
@ref s 232(6) (src:35915-35918)
GIVEN
    `the civil penalty has been imposed under section 232` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a civil penalty been imposed on the person under section 232?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 232(6) the civil penalty is to be treated as a judgment debt due to the Government` MEANS
    IF `the civil penalty has been imposed under section 232`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A civil penalty imposed under this section"

@ref s 232(6) (src:35915-35918)
GIVEN
    `the number of days the court order or the agreement allows for payment` IS A NUMBER @desc Within how many days does the court order referred to in section 232(4), or the agreement referred to in section 232(5), require the civil penalty to be paid?
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 232 to s 235 duty`
`s 232(6) the person on whom a civil penalty is imposed must pay it into the Consolidated Fund` MEANS
    PARTY Individual "the person on whom the civil penalty is imposed"
    MUST `s 232(6) pay the civil penalty into the Consolidated Fund`
    WITHIN `the number of days the court order or the agreement allows for payment`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the civil penalty was not paid into the Consolidated Fund within the time the court order or the agreement allows (section 232(6) and (7))"

-- src:35922 | (7) If the person fails to pay the civil penalty imposed on the person
-- src:35923 | within the time specified in the court order referred to in
-- src:35924 | subsection (4) or specified under the agreement referred to in
-- src:35925 | subsection (5), the Authority may recover the civil penalty on behalf
-- src:35926 | of the Government as though the civil penalty were a judgment debt
-- src:35927 | due to the Authority.
@ref s 232(7) (src:35922-35927)
GIVEN
    `the person fails to pay within the time specified in the court order referred to in subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person failed to pay the civil penalty within the time specified in the court order referred to in subsection (4)?
    `the person fails to pay within the time specified under the agreement referred to in subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person failed to pay the civil penalty within the time specified under the agreement referred to in subsection (5)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 232(7) the Authority may recover the civil penalty on behalf of the Government as though it were a judgment debt due to the Authority` MEANS
    IF `the person fails to pay within the time specified in the court order referred to in subsection (4)` OR `the person fails to pay within the time specified under the agreement referred to in subsection (5)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the Authority may recover the civil penalty on behalf of the Government" -- SPLIT-SITE (ii) [IF] -- MARGINAL-READING (a) -- GRANT-GROUP [IF-NOTHING]

-- src:35931 | (8) Any defence that is available to a person who is prosecuted for a
-- src:35932 | contravention of any provision in this Part, is also available to a
-- src:35933 | defendant to an action under this section in respect of that
-- src:35934 | contravention.
@ref s 232(8) (src:35931-35934)
GIVEN
    `a defence is available to a person prosecuted for the contravention (the answer under the section whose defence it is)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question for the defence in the prosecution answer for this person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 232(8) a defence available in a prosecution is also available to the defendant to the action` MEANS
    IF `a defence is available to a person prosecuted for the contravention (the answer under the section whose defence it is)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any defence that is available to a person who is prosecuted for a contravention of any provision in this Part, is also available"

§ `s 233: action under section 232 not to commence, etc., in certain situations`

-- src:35942 | 233.—(1) An action under section 232 must not be commenced
-- src:35943 | after the expiration of 6 years from the date of the contravention of
-- src:35944 | any of the provisions in this Part.
@ref s 233(1) (src:35942-35944)
GIVEN
    `the date of the contravention` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the person contravene the provision of Part 12?
    `the date the action under section 232 is commenced` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the action under section 232 commenced?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 233(1) the action under section 232 is barred because 6 years have expired from the date of the contravention` MEANS
    IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the date of the contravention` `the date the action under section 232 is commenced` 6 Years
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not be commenced after the expiration of 6 years from the date of the contravention" -- MARGINAL-READING (b)
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:35946 | (2) An action under section 232 must not be commenced if the
-- src:35947 | person has been convicted or acquitted in criminal proceedings for
-- src:35948 | the contravention of any of the provisions in this Part, except where
-- src:35949 | the person has been acquitted on the ground of the withdrawal of the
-- src:35950 | charge against the person.
@ref s 233(2) (src:35946-35950)
GIVEN
    `the person has been convicted in criminal proceedings for the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person been convicted in criminal proceedings for the contravention?
    `the person has been acquitted in criminal proceedings for the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person been acquitted in criminal proceedings for the contravention?
    `the person has been acquitted on the ground of the withdrawal of the charge against the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person been acquitted on the ground of the withdrawal of the charge against the person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 233(2) the action under section 232 is barred because the person has been convicted or acquitted` MEANS
    IF `the person has been convicted in criminal proceedings for the contravention` OR (`the person has been acquitted in criminal proceedings for the contravention` AND (NOT `the person has been acquitted on the ground of the withdrawal of the charge against the person`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not be commenced if the person has been convicted or acquitted in criminal proceedings" "except where the person has been acquitted on the ground of the withdrawal of the charge" -- MARGINAL-READING (a)

-- src:35952 | (3) An action under section 232 must be stayed after criminal
-- src:35953 | proceedings have been commenced against the person for the
-- src:35954 | contravention of any of the provisions in this Part, and may
-- src:35955 | thereafter be continued only if —
@ref s 233(3) (src:35952-35955)
GIVEN
    `criminal proceedings have been commenced against the person for the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have criminal proceedings been commenced against the person for the contravention of a provision of Part 12?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 233(3) the action under section 232 must be stayed` MEANS
    IF `criminal proceedings have been commenced against the person for the contravention`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "must be stayed after criminal proceedings have been commenced against the person" -- MARGINAL-READING (b)

@ref s 233(3) (src:35952-35955)
GIVEN
    `the action must be stayed (the answer under section 233(3))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question "the action under section 232 must be stayed" answer for this action? (JUST TRUE or NOTHING)
    `the person has been discharged in respect of the contravention and the discharge does not amount to an acquittal (the answer under section 233(3)(a))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question under section 233(3)(a) answer for this person? (JUST TRUE or NOTHING)
    `the charge against the person in respect of the contravention has been withdrawn (the answer under section 233(3)(b))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question under section 233(3)(b) answer for this person? (JUST TRUE or NOTHING)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 233(3) the stayed action under section 232 may thereafter be continued` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the action must be stayed (the answer under section 233(3))` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "must be stayed after criminal proceedings have been commenced against the person" -- MARGINAL-READING (b)
        IF (`the person has been discharged in respect of the contravention and the discharge does not amount to an acquittal (the answer under section 233(3)(a))` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the charge against the person in respect of the contravention has been withdrawn (the answer under section 233(3)(b))` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may thereafter be continued only if"

-- src:35957 | (a) that person has been discharged in respect of that
-- src:35958 | contravention and the discharge does not amount to an
-- src:35959 | acquittal; or
@ref s 233(3)(a) (src:35957-35959)
GIVEN
    `the person has been discharged in respect of the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person been discharged in respect of the contravention?
    `the discharge amounts to an acquittal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the discharge amount to an acquittal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 233(3)(a) the person has been discharged in respect of the contravention and the discharge does not amount to an acquittal` MEANS
    IF `the person has been discharged in respect of the contravention` AND (NOT `the discharge amounts to an acquittal`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "that person has been discharged in respect of that contravention and the discharge does not amount to an acquittal"

-- src:35961 | (b) the charge against the person in respect of that
-- src:35962 | contravention has been withdrawn.
@ref s 233(3)(b) (src:35961-35962)
GIVEN
    `the charge against the person has been withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the charge against the person in respect of the contravention been withdrawn?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 233(3)(b) the charge against the person in respect of the contravention has been withdrawn` MEANS
    IF `the charge against the person has been withdrawn`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the charge against the person in respect of that contravention has been withdrawn"

§ `s 234: civil liability`

-- src:35975 | (a) had been dealing in capital markets products of the same
-- src:35976 | description contemporaneously with the contravention;
-- src:35977 | and
@ref s 234(1)(a) (src:35975-35977)
GIVEN
    `the claimant had been dealing in capital markets products of the same description contemporaneously with the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had the claimant been dealing in capital markets products of the same description contemporaneously with the contravention? (the court takes the matters in section 234(5) into account)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 234(1)(a) the claimant had been dealing in capital markets products of the same description contemporaneously with the contravention` MEANS
    IF `the claimant had been dealing in capital markets products of the same description contemporaneously with the contravention`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "had been dealing in capital markets products of the same description contemporaneously with the contravention"

-- src:35992 | (A) in the case where the contravening person had
-- src:35993 | acted in contravention of section 218 or 219,
-- src:35994 | the information mentioned in section 218(1) or
-- src:35995 | (1A) or 219(1) (as the case may be) had been
-- src:35996 | generally available; or
@ref s 234(1)(b)(ii)(A) (src:35992-35996)
GIVEN
    `the contravening person had acted in contravention of section 218 or 219` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had the contravening person acted in contravention of section 218 or 219?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 234(1)(b)(ii)(A) the price to compare is the price had the information been generally available` MEANS
    IF `the contravening person had acted in contravention of section 218 or 219`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the case where the contravening person had acted in contravention of section 218 or 219"

-- src:35998 | (B) in any other case, the contravention had not
-- src:35999 | occurred.
@ref s 234(1)(b)(ii)(B) (src:35998-35999)
GIVEN
    `the contravening person had acted in contravention of section 218 or 219` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had the contravening person acted in contravention of section 218 or 219?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 234(1)(b)(ii)(B) the price to compare is the price had the contravention not occurred` MEANS
    IF NOT `the contravening person had acted in contravention of section 218 or 219`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in any other case"

-- src:35982 | (b) had suffered loss by reason of the difference between —
-- src:35984 | (i) the price at which the capital markets products were
-- src:35985 | dealt in contemporaneously with the contravention;
-- src:35986 | and
-- src:35988 | (ii) the price at which the capital markets products would
-- src:35989 | have been likely to have been so dealt in at the time
-- src:35990 | of the contemporaneous dealing if —
@ref s 234(1)(b) (src:35982-35990)
GIVEN
    `the claimant had suffered loss by reason of the difference between the price at which the capital markets products were dealt in contemporaneously and the price at which they would have been likely to have been so dealt in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had the claimant suffered loss by reason of the difference between (i) the price at which the capital markets products were dealt in contemporaneously with the contravention and (ii) the price at which they would have been likely to have been so dealt in at the time of the contemporaneous dealing, on the hypothesis that section 234(1)(b)(ii)(A) or (B) selects?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 234(1)(b) the claimant had suffered loss by reason of the difference in price` MEANS
    IF `the claimant had suffered loss by reason of the difference between the price at which the capital markets products were dealt in contemporaneously and the price at which they would have been likely to have been so dealt in`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "had suffered loss by reason of the difference between"

-- src:35966 | 234.—(1) A person who has acted in contravention of any of the
-- src:35967 | provisions in this Part (called in this section and sections 235 and 236
-- src:35968 | the contravening person) is, if the contravening person had gained a
-- src:35969 | profit or avoided a loss as a result of that contravention, whether or
-- src:35970 | not the contravening person had been convicted or had a civil penalty
-- src:35971 | imposed on the contravening person in respect of that contravention,
-- src:35972 | liable to pay compensation to any person (called in this section and
-- src:35973 | sections 235 and 236 the claimant) who —
@ref s 234(1) (src:35966-35973)
GIVEN
    `the contravening person has acted in contravention of a provision of Part 12 (the answer under the section contravened)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question under the section of Part 12 that the person is said to have contravened answer for this person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING)
    `the contravening person had gained a profit or avoided a loss as a result of the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had the contravening person gained a profit or avoided a loss as a result of the contravention?
    `the claimant had been dealing contemporaneously (the answer under section 234(1)(a))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question under section 234(1)(a) answer for this claimant? (JUST TRUE or NOTHING)
    `the claimant had suffered loss by reason of the difference in price (the answer under section 234(1)(b))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question under section 234(1)(b) answer for this claimant? (JUST TRUE or NOTHING)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 234(1) the contravening person is liable to pay compensation to the claimant` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the contravening person has acted in contravention of a provision of Part 12 (the answer under the section contravened)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who has acted in contravention of any of the provisions in this Part" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [OWN]
        IF NOT `the contravening person had gained a profit or avoided a loss as a result of the contravention`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is, if the contravening person had gained a profit or avoided a loss as a result of that contravention" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [IF] -- MARGINAL-READING (a) -- GRANT-GROUP [ENTITLED]
        IF (`the claimant had been dealing contemporaneously (the answer under section 234(1)(a))` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`the claimant had suffered loss by reason of the difference in price (the answer under section 234(1)(b))` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "liable to pay compensation to any person" "(called in this section and sections 235 and 236 the claimant) who" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [OWN] -- MARGINAL-READING (b)

-- src:36010 | (a) the contravening person has contravened section 199, 200
-- src:36011 | or 201 in connection with any dealing in capital markets
-- src:36012 | products, by —
-- src:36014 | (i) making, disseminating or publishing any false,
-- src:36015 | misleading or deceptive statement, information,
-- src:36016 | promise or forecast; or
-- src:36018 | (ii) concealing or omitting to state any material fact; and
@ref s 234(1A)(a) (src:36010-36018)
GIVEN
    `the contravening person has contravened section 199, 200 or 201 in connection with a dealing in capital markets products` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the contravening person contravened section 199, 200 or 201 in connection with any dealing in capital markets products?
    `the contravention was by making, disseminating or publishing a false, misleading or deceptive statement, information, promise or forecast` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the contravention by making, disseminating or publishing any false, misleading or deceptive statement, information, promise or forecast?
    `the contravention was by concealing or omitting to state a material fact` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the contravention by concealing or omitting to state any material fact?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 234(1A)(a) the contravening person has contravened section 199, 200 or 201 by a false statement or a concealed fact` MEANS
    IF `the contravening person has contravened section 199, 200 or 201 in connection with a dealing in capital markets products` AND (`the contravention was by making, disseminating or publishing a false, misleading or deceptive statement, information, promise or forecast` OR `the contravention was by concealing or omitting to state a material fact`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "has contravened section 199, 200 or 201 in connection with any dealing in capital markets products, by"

-- src:36020 | (b) the claimant —
-- src:36022 | (i) in reliance on that statement, information, promise or
-- src:36023 | forecast or in ignorance of that concealed or omitted
-- src:36024 | material fact, had (whether contemporaneously with
-- src:36025 | the contravention or otherwise) been dealing in
-- src:36026 | capital markets products of the same description; and
-- src:36031 | (ii) had suffered loss.
@ref s 234(1A)(b) (src:36020-36031)
GIVEN
    `the claimant, in reliance on the statement, information, promise or forecast or in ignorance of the concealed or omitted material fact, had been dealing in capital markets products of the same description` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had the claimant, in reliance on that statement, information, promise or forecast or in ignorance of that concealed or omitted material fact, been dealing (whether contemporaneously with the contravention or otherwise) in capital markets products of the same description?
    `the claimant had suffered loss` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had the claimant suffered loss?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 234(1A)(b) the claimant relied on the statement or was ignorant of the fact, and suffered loss` MEANS
    IF `the claimant, in reliance on the statement, information, promise or forecast or in ignorance of the concealed or omitted material fact, had been dealing in capital markets products of the same description` AND `the claimant had suffered loss`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the claimant" "in reliance on that statement, information, promise or forecast or in ignorance of that concealed or omitted material fact"

-- src:36003 | (1A) Without affecting subsection (1), the contravening person is,
-- src:36004 | whether or not the contravening person had gained a profit or avoided
-- src:36005 | a loss as a result of that contravention, and whether or not the
-- src:36006 | contravening person had been convicted or had a civil penalty
-- src:36007 | imposed on the contravening person in respect of that contravention,
-- src:36008 | liable to pay compensation to the claimant, if —
@ref s 234(1A) (src:36003-36008)
GIVEN
    `the contravening person has acted in contravention of section 199, 200 or 201 (the answer under the section contravened)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question under section 199, 200 or 201 that the person is said to have contravened answer for this person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING)
    `the contravention was by a false statement or a concealed fact (the answer under section 234(1A)(a))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question under section 234(1A)(a) answer for this person? (JUST TRUE or NOTHING)
    `the claimant relied on the statement or was ignorant of the fact, and suffered loss (the answer under section 234(1A)(b))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question under section 234(1A)(b) answer for this claimant? (JUST TRUE or NOTHING)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 234(1A) the contravening person is liable to pay compensation to the claimant whether or not the person gained a profit or avoided a loss` MEANS
    IF (`the contravening person has acted in contravention of section 199, 200 or 201 (the answer under the section contravened)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`the contravention was by a false statement or a concealed fact (the answer under section 234(1A)(a))` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`the claimant relied on the statement or was ignorant of the fact, and suffered loss (the answer under section 234(1A)(b))` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the contravening person is, whether or not the contravening person had gained a profit or avoided a loss as a result of that contravention" "liable to pay compensation to the claimant, if" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [OWN] -- MARGINAL-READING (b)

-- src:36035 | (2) The amount of compensation that the contravening person is
-- src:36036 | liable to pay to the claimant under subsection (1) is the amount of the
-- src:36037 | loss suffered by the claimant referred to in subsection (1)(b), after
-- src:36038 | deducting any amount of compensation paid or payable to the same
-- src:36039 | claimant in respect of the same contravention under an order of court
-- src:36040 | or an agreement to pay by the contravening person or any defendant,
-- src:36041 | defendant corporation or defendant partnership under Division 4 or 5
-- src:36042 | or under an order for disgorgement under section 236L, up to the
-- src:36043 | maximum amount recoverable.
@ref s 234(2) (src:36035-36043)
GIVEN
    `the amount of the loss suffered by the claimant referred to in subsection (1)(b)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the loss suffered by the claimant referred to in section 234(1)(b)?
    `the compensation paid or payable to the same claimant in respect of the same contravention` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total of the compensation paid or payable to the same claimant in respect of the same contravention under an order of court or an agreement to pay by the contravening person or any defendant, defendant corporation or defendant partnership under Division 4 or 5, or under an order for disgorgement under section 236L? (0 if none)
    `the maximum amount recoverable (the answer under section 234(6))` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum amount recoverable under section 234(6) for this contravention?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 234(2) the amount of compensation under subsection (1)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the amount of the loss suffered by the claimant referred to in subsection (1)(b)` MINUS `the compensation paid or payable to the same claimant in respect of the same contravention` AT MOST 0
        THEN 0  -- FORK F-234-2: a negative result after deduction is read as nothing owed
        IF `the amount of the loss suffered by the claimant referred to in subsection (1)(b)` MINUS `the compensation paid or payable to the same claimant in respect of the same contravention` GREATER THAN `the maximum amount recoverable (the answer under section 234(6))`
        THEN `the maximum amount recoverable (the answer under section 234(6))`  -- "up to the maximum amount recoverable"
        OTHERWISE `the amount of the loss suffered by the claimant referred to in subsection (1)(b)` MINUS `the compensation paid or payable to the same claimant in respect of the same contravention`

-- src:36056 | (i) the amount of the loss suffered by the claimant
-- src:36057 | referred to in subsection (1)(b), after deducting any
-- src:36058 | amount of compensation paid or payable to the same
-- src:36059 | claimant in respect of the same contravention under
-- src:36060 | an order of court or an agreement to pay by the
-- src:36061 | contravening person or any defendant, defendant
-- src:36062 | corporation or defendant partnership under
-- src:36063 | Division 4 or 5 or under an order for disgorgement
-- src:36064 | under section 236L, up to the maximum amount
-- src:36065 | recoverable;
@ref s 234(2A)(a)(i) (src:36056-36065)
GIVEN
    `the amount of the loss suffered by the claimant referred to in subsection (1)(b)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the loss suffered by the claimant referred to in section 234(1)(b)?
    `the compensation paid or payable to the same claimant in respect of the same contravention` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total of the compensation paid or payable to the same claimant in respect of the same contravention under an order of court or an agreement to pay by the contravening person or any defendant, defendant corporation or defendant partnership under Division 4 or 5, or under an order for disgorgement under section 236L? (0 if none)
    `the maximum amount recoverable (the answer under section 234(6))` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum amount recoverable under section 234(6) for this contravention?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 234(2A)(a)(i) the amount of the loss referred to in subsection (1)(b)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the amount of the loss suffered by the claimant referred to in subsection (1)(b)` MINUS `the compensation paid or payable to the same claimant in respect of the same contravention` AT MOST 0
        THEN 0  -- FORK F-234-2: a negative result after deduction is read as nothing owed
        IF `the amount of the loss suffered by the claimant referred to in subsection (1)(b)` MINUS `the compensation paid or payable to the same claimant in respect of the same contravention` GREATER THAN `the maximum amount recoverable (the answer under section 234(6))`
        THEN `the maximum amount recoverable (the answer under section 234(6))`  -- "up to the maximum amount recoverable"
        OTHERWISE `the amount of the loss suffered by the claimant referred to in subsection (1)(b)` MINUS `the compensation paid or payable to the same claimant in respect of the same contravention`

-- src:36067 | (ii) the amount of any loss that reasonably results from
-- src:36068 | the claimant’s reliance on the statement, information,
-- src:36069 | promise or forecast referred to in
-- src:36070 | subsection (1A)(a)(i) or ignorance of the concealed
-- src:36071 | or omitted material fact referred to in
-- src:36072 | subsection (1A)(a)(ii), after deducting any amount
-- src:36073 | of compensation paid or payable to the same
-- src:36074 | claimant in respect of the same contravention
-- src:36079 | under an order of court or an agreement to pay by the
-- src:36080 | contravening person or any defendant, defendant
-- src:36081 | corporation or defendant partnership under
-- src:36082 | Division 4 or 5 or under an order for disgorgement
-- src:36083 | under section 236L; or
@ref s 234(2A)(a)(ii) (src:36067-36083)
GIVEN
    `the amount of the loss that reasonably results from the claimant's reliance or ignorance` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of any loss that reasonably results from the claimant's reliance on the statement, information, promise or forecast referred to in section 234(1A)(a)(i), or ignorance of the concealed or omitted material fact referred to in section 234(1A)(a)(ii)?
    `the compensation paid or payable to the same claimant in respect of the same contravention` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total of the compensation paid or payable to the same claimant in respect of the same contravention under an order of court or an agreement to pay by the contravening person or any defendant, defendant corporation or defendant partnership under Division 4 or 5, or under an order for disgorgement under section 236L? (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 234(2A)(a)(ii) the amount of the loss that reasonably results from the claimant's reliance or ignorance` MEANS
    IF `the amount of the loss that reasonably results from the claimant's reliance or ignorance` MINUS `the compensation paid or payable to the same claimant in respect of the same contravention` AT MOST 0
    THEN 0  -- FORK F-234-2: a negative result after deduction is read as nothing owed
    ELSE `the amount of the loss that reasonably results from the claimant's reliance or ignorance` MINUS `the compensation paid or payable to the same claimant in respect of the same contravention`  -- the text states no cap for this amount: only paragraph (a)(i) says "up to the maximum amount recoverable"

-- src:36085 | (b) in any other case, the amount of any loss that reasonably
-- src:36086 | results from the claimant’s reliance on the statement,
-- src:36087 | information, promise or forecast referred to in
-- src:36088 | subsection (1A)(a)(i) or ignorance of the concealed or
-- src:36089 | omitted material fact referred to in subsection (1A)(a)(ii),
-- src:36090 | after deducting any amount of compensation paid or
-- src:36091 | payable to the same claimant in respect of the same
-- src:36092 | contravention under an order of court or an agreement to
-- src:36093 | pay by the contravening person or any defendant,
-- src:36094 | defendant corporation or defendant partnership under
-- src:36095 | Division 4 or 5 or under an order for disgorgement under
-- src:36096 | section 236L.
@ref s 234(2A)(b) (src:36085-36096)
GIVEN
    `the amount of the loss that reasonably results from the claimant's reliance or ignorance` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of any loss that reasonably results from the claimant's reliance on the statement, information, promise or forecast referred to in section 234(1A)(a)(i), or ignorance of the concealed or omitted material fact referred to in section 234(1A)(a)(ii)?
    `the compensation paid or payable to the same claimant in respect of the same contravention` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total of the compensation paid or payable to the same claimant in respect of the same contravention under an order of court or an agreement to pay by the contravening person or any defendant, defendant corporation or defendant partnership under Division 4 or 5, or under an order for disgorgement under section 236L? (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 234(2A)(b) the amount of the loss that reasonably results from the claimant's reliance or ignorance in any other case` MEANS
    IF `the amount of the loss that reasonably results from the claimant's reliance or ignorance` MINUS `the compensation paid or payable to the same claimant in respect of the same contravention` AT MOST 0
    THEN 0  -- FORK F-234-2: a negative result after deduction is read as nothing owed
    ELSE `the amount of the loss that reasonably results from the claimant's reliance or ignorance` MINUS `the compensation paid or payable to the same claimant in respect of the same contravention`

-- src:36047 | (2A) The amount of compensation that the contravening person is
-- src:36048 | liable to pay to the claimant under subsection (1A) is —
-- src:36050 | (a) in any case where the claimant had contemporaneously
-- src:36051 | with the contravention been dealing in capital markets
-- src:36052 | products of the same description, and had suffered the loss
-- src:36053 | referred to in subsection (1)(b), any one of the following
-- src:36054 | amounts that is elected by the claimant:
@ref s 234(2A) (src:36047-36054)
GIVEN
    `the claimant had contemporaneously with the contravention been dealing in capital markets products of the same description, and had suffered the loss referred to in subsection (1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had the claimant, contemporaneously with the contravention, been dealing in capital markets products of the same description, and suffered the loss referred to in section 234(1)(b)?
    `the claimant elects the amount in paragraph (a)(i)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the claimant elect the amount in section 234(2A)(a)(i) (the loss referred to in section 234(1)(b)) rather than the amount in section 234(2A)(a)(ii)?
    `the amount in paragraph (a)(i) (the answer under section 234(2A)(a)(i))` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the answer under section 234(2A)(a)(i) for this claimant?
    `the amount in paragraph (a)(ii) (the answer under section 234(2A)(a)(ii))` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the answer under section 234(2A)(a)(ii) for this claimant?
    `the amount in paragraph (b) (the answer under section 234(2A)(b))` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the answer under section 234(2A)(b) for this claimant?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 234(2A) the amount of compensation under subsection (1A)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the claimant had contemporaneously with the contravention been dealing in capital markets products of the same description, and had suffered the loss referred to in subsection (1)(b)` AND `the claimant elects the amount in paragraph (a)(i)`
        THEN `the amount in paragraph (a)(i) (the answer under section 234(2A)(a)(i))`
        IF `the claimant had contemporaneously with the contravention been dealing in capital markets products of the same description, and had suffered the loss referred to in subsection (1)(b)`
        THEN `the amount in paragraph (a)(ii) (the answer under section 234(2A)(a)(ii))`  -- "any one of the following amounts that is elected by the claimant": the claimant who does not elect (a)(i) takes (a)(ii)
        OTHERWISE `the amount in paragraph (b) (the answer under section 234(2A)(b))`

-- src:36100 | (3) Any defence that is available to a person who is prosecuted for a
-- src:36101 | contravention of any provision in this Part, is also available to a
-- src:36102 | defendant to an action under this section in respect of the
-- src:36103 | contravention.
@ref s 234(3) (src:36100-36103)
GIVEN
    `a defence is available to a person prosecuted for the contravention (the answer under the section whose defence it is)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question for the defence in the prosecution answer for this person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 234(3) a defence available in a prosecution is also available to the defendant to the action` MEANS
    IF `a defence is available to a person prosecuted for the contravention (the answer under the section whose defence it is)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any defence that is available to a person who is prosecuted for a contravention of any provision in this Part, is also available"

-- src:36105 | (4) An action under this section must not be commenced after the
-- src:36106 | expiration of 6 years from the date of completion of the dealing in
-- src:36107 | which the loss occurred.
@ref s 234(4) (src:36105-36107)
GIVEN
    `the date of completion of the dealing in which the loss occurred` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the dealing in which the loss occurred completed?
    `the date the action under section 234 is commenced` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the action under section 234 commenced?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 234(4) the action under section 234 is barred because 6 years have expired from the date of completion of the dealing` MEANS
    IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the date of completion of the dealing in which the loss occurred` `the date the action under section 234 is commenced` 6 Years
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not be commenced after the expiration of 6 years from the date of completion of the dealing in which the loss occurred" -- MARGINAL-READING (b)
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:36111 | (5) For the purposes of this section, in determining whether any
-- src:36112 | dealing in capital markets products took place contemporaneously
-- src:36113 | with the contravention, the court is to take into account the following
-- src:36114 | matters:
@ref s 234(5) (src:36111-36114)
GIVEN
    `this section or section 236 is applied to decide whether a dealing took place contemporaneously with the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court deciding, for the purposes of section 234, whether any dealing in capital markets products took place contemporaneously with the contravention?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 234(5) the court is to take into account the matters in paragraphs (a) to (e)` MEANS
    IF `this section or section 236 is applied to decide whether a dealing took place contemporaneously with the contravention`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purposes of this section, in determining whether any dealing in capital markets products took place contemporaneously with the contravention"

-- src:36116 | (a) the volume of capital markets products of the same
-- src:36117 | description dealt in between the date and time of the
-- src:36118 | contravention, and the date and time of the dealing in
-- src:36119 | capital markets products;
@ref s 234(5)(a) (src:36116-36119)
GIVEN
    `the matter is the volume of capital markets products of the same description dealt in between the date and time of the contravention and the date and time of the dealing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter the volume of capital markets products of the same description dealt in between the date and time of the contravention and the date and time of the dealing in capital markets products?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 234(5)(a) the matter is one the court is to take into account` MEANS
    IF `the matter is the volume of capital markets products of the same description dealt in between the date and time of the contravention and the date and time of the dealing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the volume of capital markets products of the same description dealt in between the date and time of the contravention"

-- src:36121 | (b) if the contravention was effected by a transaction or
-- src:36122 | transactions involving the dealing in capital markets
-- src:36127 | products, the date on and time at which the transaction or
-- src:36128 | transactions were cleared and settled;
@ref s 234(5)(b) (src:36121-36128)
GIVEN
    `the contravention was effected by a transaction or transactions involving the dealing in capital markets products` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the contravention effected by a transaction or transactions involving the dealing in capital markets products?
    `the matter is the date on and time at which the transactions were cleared and settled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter the date on and time at which the transaction or transactions were cleared and settled?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 234(5)(b) the matter is one the court is to take into account in the case of a contravention effected by a transaction` MEANS
    IF `the contravention was effected by a transaction or transactions involving the dealing in capital markets products` AND `the matter is the date on and time at which the transactions were cleared and settled`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the contravention was effected by a transaction or transactions involving the dealing in capital markets products"

-- src:36130 | (c) whether the dealing in capital markets products took place
-- src:36131 | before or after the contravention;
@ref s 234(5)(c) (src:36130-36131)
GIVEN
    `the matter is whether the dealing in capital markets products took place before or after the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter whether the dealing in capital markets products took place before or after the contravention?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 234(5)(c) the matter is one the court is to take into account` MEANS
    IF `the matter is whether the dealing in capital markets products took place before or after the contravention`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "whether the dealing in capital markets products took place before or after the contravention"

-- src:36133 | (d) in the case of a contravention under section 203, 218 or
-- src:36134 | 219, whether the dealing in capital markets products that
-- src:36135 | are securities, securities‑based derivatives contracts or CIS
-- src:36136 | units as defined in section 214(1) (as the case may be) took
-- src:36137 | place before or after the information to which the
-- src:36138 | contravention relates became generally known;
@ref s 234(5)(d) (src:36133-36138)
GIVEN
    `the contravention is a contravention under section 203, 218 or 219` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contravention a contravention under section 203, 218 or 219?
    `the dealing is in securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or CIS units as defined in section 214(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the dealing in capital markets products that are securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or CIS units as defined in section 214(1) (as the case may be)?
    `the matter is whether the dealing took place before or after the information to which the contravention relates became generally known` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter whether the dealing took place before or after the information to which the contravention relates became generally known?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 234(5)(d) the matter is one the court is to take into account in the case of a contravention under section 203, 218 or 219` MEANS
    IF `the contravention is a contravention under section 203, 218 or 219` AND `the dealing is in securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or CIS units as defined in section 214(1)` AND `the matter is whether the dealing took place before or after the information to which the contravention relates became generally known`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the case of a contravention under section 203, 218 or 219"

-- src:36140 | (e) such other factors and developments, whether in Singapore
-- src:36141 | or elsewhere, as the court may consider relevant.
@ref s 234(5)(e) (src:36140-36141)
GIVEN
    `the matter is another factor or development, in Singapore or elsewhere, that the court considers relevant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter another factor or development, whether in Singapore or elsewhere, that the court considers relevant?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 234(5)(e) the matter is one the court is to take into account` MEANS
    IF `the matter is another factor or development, in Singapore or elsewhere, that the court considers relevant`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such other factors and developments, whether in Singapore or elsewhere, as the court may consider relevant"

-- src:36145 | (6) In this section and section 236, “maximum recoverable
-- src:36146 | amount”, in respect of each contravention by a contravening
-- src:36147 | person means —
-- src:36149 | (a) the amount of the profit that the contravening person
-- src:36150 | gained; or
-- src:36152 | (b) the amount of the loss that the contravening person
-- src:36153 | avoided,
-- src:36155 | as a result of the contravention, after deducting all amounts of
-- src:36156 | compensation that the contravening person had previously been
-- src:36157 | ordered by a court to pay, in respect of the same contravention, to
-- src:36158 | other claimants (each being a claimant whose claim is one where the
-- src:36159 | amount of compensation that the contravening person is liable to pay
-- src:36160 | is specified under subsection (2) or (2A)(a)(i)).
@ref s 234(6) (src:36145-36160)
GIVEN
    `the amount of the profit that the contravening person gained` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the profit that the contravening person gained as a result of the contravention? (0 if none)
    `the amount of the loss that the contravening person avoided` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the loss that the contravening person avoided as a result of the contravention? (0 if none)
    `the compensation previously ordered by a court to be paid to other claimants in respect of the same contravention` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total of the compensation that the contravening person had previously been ordered by a court to pay, in respect of the same contravention, to other claimants whose compensation is specified under section 234(2) or (2A)(a)(i)? (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 234(6) the maximum recoverable amount` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the amount of the profit that the contravening person gained` GREATER THAN `the amount of the loss that the contravening person avoided`) AND (`the amount of the profit that the contravening person gained` MINUS `the compensation previously ordered by a court to be paid to other claimants in respect of the same contravention` GREATER THAN 0)
        THEN `the amount of the profit that the contravening person gained` MINUS `the compensation previously ordered by a court to be paid to other claimants in respect of the same contravention`  -- FORK F-234-6: "(a) the profit gained; or (b) the loss avoided" read as the greater of the two when both are present
        IF (NOT (`the amount of the profit that the contravening person gained` GREATER THAN `the amount of the loss that the contravening person avoided`)) AND (`the amount of the loss that the contravening person avoided` MINUS `the compensation previously ordered by a court to be paid to other claimants in respect of the same contravention` GREATER THAN 0)
        THEN `the amount of the loss that the contravening person avoided` MINUS `the compensation previously ordered by a court to be paid to other claimants in respect of the same contravention`
        OTHERWISE 0  -- FORK F-234-6: a negative result after deduction is read as nothing recoverable

§ `s 235: action under section 234 not to commence, etc., in certain situations`

-- src:36167 | 235.—(1) Except with the permission of court, no action under
-- src:36168 | section 234 may be brought against the contravening person in
-- src:36169 | respect of a contravention of any of the provisions in this Part which
-- src:36170 | resulted in the contravening person gaining a profit or avoiding a loss
-- src:36171 | after the commencement of —
-- src:36176 | (a) criminal proceedings under this Part against the
-- src:36177 | contravening person for the same contravention; or
-- src:36179 | (b) an action under section 232 against the contravening
-- src:36180 | person for the same contravention.
@ref s 235(1) (src:36167-36180)
GIVEN
    `the contravention resulted in the contravening person gaining a profit or avoiding a loss` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the contravention result in the contravening person gaining a profit or avoiding a loss?
    `the action under section 234 is brought after the commencement of criminal proceedings under Part 12 against the contravening person for the same contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the action under section 234 brought after the commencement of criminal proceedings under Part 12 against the contravening person for the same contravention?
    `the action under section 234 is brought after the commencement of an action under section 232 against the contravening person for the same contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the action under section 234 brought after the commencement of an action under section 232 against the contravening person for the same contravention?
    `the court has given permission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court given permission for the action?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 235(1) no action under section 234 may be brought without the permission of court` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the contravention resulted in the contravening person gaining a profit or avoiding a loss`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in respect of a contravention of any of the provisions in this Part which resulted in the contravening person gaining a profit or avoiding a loss" -- MARGINAL-READING (b)
        IF NOT (`the action under section 234 is brought after the commencement of criminal proceedings under Part 12 against the contravening person for the same contravention` OR `the action under section 234 is brought after the commencement of an action under section 232 against the contravening person for the same contravention`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "after the commencement of" -- MARGINAL-READING (b) -- FORK F-235-1: "after the commencement of" read as qualifying when the action is brought
        IF `the court has given permission`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Except with the permission of court" -- MARGINAL-READING (a)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:36184 | (2) Any action under section 234 against the contravening person in
-- src:36185 | respect of a contravention of any of the provisions in this Part which
-- src:36186 | resulted in the contravening person gaining a profit or avoiding a loss,
-- src:36187 | being an action that is pending on the date of commencement of —
-- src:36189 | (a) criminal proceedings under this Part against the
-- src:36190 | contravening person for the same contravention; or
-- src:36192 | (b) an action under section 232 against the contravening
-- src:36193 | person for the same contravention,
-- src:36195 | must be stayed, and may not thereafter be continued except with the
-- src:36196 | permission of court.
@ref s 235(2) (src:36184-36196)
GIVEN
    `the contravention resulted in the contravening person gaining a profit or avoiding a loss` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the contravention result in the contravening person gaining a profit or avoiding a loss?
    `the action under section 234 is pending on the date of commencement of criminal proceedings under Part 12 against the contravening person for the same contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the action under section 234 pending on the date of commencement of criminal proceedings under Part 12 against the contravening person for the same contravention?
    `the action under section 234 is pending on the date of commencement of an action under section 232 against the contravening person for the same contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the action under section 234 pending on the date of commencement of an action under section 232 against the contravening person for the same contravention?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 235(2) the pending action under section 234 must be stayed` MEANS
    IF `the contravention resulted in the contravening person gaining a profit or avoiding a loss` AND (`the action under section 234 is pending on the date of commencement of criminal proceedings under Part 12 against the contravening person for the same contravention` OR `the action under section 234 is pending on the date of commencement of an action under section 232 against the contravening person for the same contravention`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "being an action that is pending on the date of commencement of" -- MARGINAL-READING (b)

@ref s 235(2) (src:36184-36196)
GIVEN
    `the action must be stayed (the answer under section 235(2))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question "the pending action under section 234 must be stayed" answer for this action? (JUST TRUE or NOTHING)
    `the court has given permission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court given permission for the action?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 235(2) the stayed action may thereafter be continued` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the action must be stayed (the answer under section 235(2))` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "must be stayed, and may not thereafter be continued except with the permission of court" -- MARGINAL-READING (b)
        IF `the court has given permission`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may not thereafter be continued except with the permission of court"

-- src:36200 | (3) Permission under subsection (1) or (2) may not be granted if a
-- src:36201 | date has been fixed by a court under section 236(1) for the filing of
-- src:36202 | claims, and in that event the claimant to the proposed action or the
-- src:36203 | action that has been stayed (as the case may be) must comply with
-- src:36204 | such directions relating to the filing and proof of the claimant’s claim
-- src:36205 | under section 236 as that court may issue in the claimant’s case.
@ref s 235(3) (src:36200-36205)
GIVEN
    `a date has been fixed by a court under section 236(1) for the filing of claims` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a date been fixed by a court under section 236(1) for the filing of claims?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 235(3) permission under subsection (1) or (2) may be granted` MEANS
    IF `a date has been fixed by a court under section 236(1) for the filing of claims`
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Permission under subsection (1) or (2) may not be granted if a date has been fixed by a court under section 236(1) for the filing of claims"
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not itself say when permission may be granted

@ref s 235(3) (src:36200-36205)
GIVEN
    `the number of days the court's directions allow for the filing and proof of the claim` IS A NUMBER @desc Within how many days do the directions that the court issues in the claimant's case require the claim to be filed and proved?
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 232 to s 235 duty`
`s 235(3) the claimant must comply with the court's directions on the filing and proof of the claim` MEANS
    PARTY Individual "the claimant"
    MUST `s 235(3) comply with the court's directions on the filing and proof of the claim under section 236`
    WITHIN `the number of days the court's directions allow for the filing and proof of the claim`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the claimant did not file and prove the claim within the time the court's directions allow (section 235(3))"

DECLARE `s 232 to s 235 duty` IS ONE OF
    `s 232(6) pay the civil penalty into the Consolidated Fund`
    `s 235(3) comply with the court's directions on the filing and proof of the claim under section 236`

§ `s 236: civil liability in event of conviction, etc.`

-- src:36268 | (4) For the purposes of this section, a conviction is made final if —
-- src:36270 | (a) the conviction is upheld on appeal, revision or otherwise;
-- src:36272 | (b) the conviction is not subject to further appeal;
-- src:36277 | (c) no notice of appeal against the conviction is lodged within
-- src:36278 | the time prescribed by sections 377 and 378 of the
-- src:36279 | Criminal Procedure Code 2010; or
-- src:36281 | (d) any appeal against the conviction is withdrawn.
@ref s 236(4) (src:36268-36281)
GIVEN
    `the conviction is upheld on appeal, revision or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the conviction upheld on appeal, revision or otherwise?
    `the conviction is not subject to further appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the conviction not subject to further appeal?
    `no notice of appeal against the conviction is lodged within the time prescribed by sections 377 and 378 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that no notice of appeal against the conviction is lodged within the time prescribed by sections 377 and 378 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010? (that Code is not among the sources)
    `any appeal against the conviction is withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is any appeal against the conviction withdrawn?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236(4) the conviction is made final` MEANS
    IF `the conviction is upheld on appeal, revision or otherwise` OR `the conviction is not subject to further appeal` OR `no notice of appeal against the conviction is lodged within the time prescribed by sections 377 and 378 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010` OR `any appeal against the conviction is withdrawn`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a conviction is made final if" -- MARGINAL-READING (a)

-- src:36285 | (5) For the purposes of this section, an order imposing a civil
-- src:36286 | penalty is made final if —
-- src:36288 | (a) the order is not set aside on appeal or revision or is varied
-- src:36289 | only as to the amount of the civil penalty to be imposed;
-- src:36291 | (b) the order is not subject to further appeal;
-- src:36293 | (c) no notice of appeal against the imposition of the penalty is
-- src:36294 | lodged within the time prescribed by Rules of Court made
-- src:36295 | under section 238; or
-- src:36297 | (d) any appeal against the imposition of the penalty is
-- src:36298 | withdrawn.
@ref s 236(5) (src:36285-36298)
GIVEN
    `the order is not set aside on appeal or revision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order not set aside on appeal or revision?
    `the order is varied only as to the amount of the civil penalty to be imposed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order varied only as to the amount of the civil penalty to be imposed?
    `the order is not subject to further appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order not subject to further appeal?
    `no notice of appeal against the imposition of the penalty is lodged within the time prescribed by Rules of Court made under section 238` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that no notice of appeal against the imposition of the penalty is lodged within the time prescribed by Rules of Court made under section 238? (the Rules are not among the sources)
    `any appeal against the imposition of the penalty is withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is any appeal against the imposition of the penalty withdrawn?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236(5) the order imposing a civil penalty is made final` MEANS
    IF `the order is not set aside on appeal or revision` OR `the order is varied only as to the amount of the civil penalty to be imposed` OR `the order is not subject to further appeal` OR `no notice of appeal against the imposition of the penalty is lodged within the time prescribed by Rules of Court made under section 238` OR `any appeal against the imposition of the penalty is withdrawn`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an order imposing a civil penalty is made final if" -- MARGINAL-READING (a)

-- src:36211 | 236.—(1) Despite section 234, where the contravening person —
-- src:36213 | (a) has been convicted of an offence under this Part; or
-- src:36215 | (b) has an order for the payment of a civil penalty made against
-- src:36216 | the contravening person under section 232, other than by
-- src:36217 | way of a default judgment or a consent order made with or
-- src:36218 | without admission of contravention under section 232(4),
-- src:36220 | in respect of the contravention of any of the provisions in this Part, the
-- src:36221 | court which convicted the contravening person or made the order
-- src:36222 | against the contravening person (called in this section the relevant
-- src:36223 | court) may, after the conviction or the order imposing the civil
-- src:36228 | penalty has been made final, fix a date on or before which all
-- src:36229 | claimants have to file and prove their claims for compensation in
-- src:36230 | respect of that contravention.
@ref s 236(1) (src:36211-36230)
GIVEN
    `the contravening person has been convicted of an offence under Part 12` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the contravening person been convicted of an offence under Part 12?
    `the contravening person has an order for the payment of a civil penalty made against the person under section 232` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an order for the payment of a civil penalty been made against the contravening person under section 232?
    `the order was made by way of a default judgment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that order made by way of a default judgment?
    `the order was a consent order made with or without admission of contravention under section 232(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that order a consent order made with or without admission of contravention under section 232(4)?
    `the conviction or the order has been made final (the answer under section 236(4) or (5))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question under section 236(4) (conviction) or section 236(5) (order) answer for this person? (JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236(1) the relevant court may fix a date on or before which all claimants have to file and prove their claims` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the contravening person has been convicted of an offence under Part 12` OR (`the contravening person has an order for the payment of a civil penalty made against the person under section 232` AND (NOT `the order was made by way of a default judgment`) AND (NOT `the order was a consent order made with or without admission of contravention under section 232(4)`)))
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the contravening person" "has been convicted of an offence under this Part" "other than by way of a default judgment or a consent order" -- SPLIT-SITE (ii) [WHERE] -- GRANT-GROUP [WHERE-LISTED]
        IF NOT (`the conviction or the order has been made final (the answer under section 236(4) or (5))` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "after the conviction or the order imposing the civil penalty has been made final" -- SPLIT-SITE (ii) [AFTER] -- MARGINAL-READING (b)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:36234 | (2) For the purposes of subsection (1), the relevant court must not
-- src:36235 | fix a date that is earlier than 3 months from the date the conviction or
-- src:36236 | the order imposing the civil penalty (as the case may be) has been
-- src:36237 | made final.
@ref s 236(2) (src:36234-36237)
GIVEN
    `the date the conviction or the order imposing the civil penalty was made final` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the conviction, or the order imposing the civil penalty, made final?
    `the date the relevant court fixes for the filing of claims` IS A DATE @desc What date does the relevant court fix for the filing and proof of claims?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236(2) the date fixed is not earlier than 3 months from the date the conviction or the order was made final` MEANS
    IF `the date the relevant court fixes for the filing of claims` AT LEAST `period: the last day of a period after` `the date the conviction or the order imposing the civil penalty was made final` 3 Months
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the relevant court must not fix a date that is earlier than 3 months from the date"

-- src:36239 | (3) Subject to subsection (3A), the relevant court may, after the
-- src:36240 | expiry of the date fixed under subsection (1), make an order against
-- src:36241 | the contravening person to pay compensation to each claimant who
-- src:36242 | has filed and proven that claimant’s claim for compensation.
@ref s 236(3) (src:36239-36242)
GIVEN
    `the date fixed under section 236(1) has expired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the date fixed under section 236(1) for the filing and proof of claims expired?
    `the claimant has filed and proven the claimant's claim for compensation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the claimant filed and proven the claimant's claim for compensation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236(3) the relevant court may make an order against the contravening person to pay compensation to the claimant` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the date fixed under section 236(1) has expired`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may, after the expiry of the date fixed under subsection (1), make an order" -- SPLIT-SITE (ii) [AFTER] -- MARGINAL-READING (b)
        IF NOT `the claimant has filed and proven the claimant's claim for compensation`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to each claimant who has filed and proven that claimant's claim for compensation" -- SPLIT-SITE (ii) [WHO] -- MARGINAL-READING (b)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:36246 | (3A) Where the amount of compensation that a claimant would
-- src:36247 | have been entitled if the claimant had brought an action under
-- src:36248 | section 234 is specified under section 234(2) or (2A)(a)(i), the
-- src:36249 | compensation amount ordered by the relevant court for that claimant
-- src:36250 | is equal to the lesser of the following amounts:
-- src:36252 | (a) the amount of compensation which that claimant has
-- src:36253 | proven to the satisfaction of the court that the claimant
-- src:36254 | would have been entitled to if the claimant had brought an
-- src:36255 | action under section 234 against the contravening person;
-- src:36257 | (b) the pro‑rated portion of the maximum recoverable amount,
-- src:36258 | calculated according to the relationship which the amount
-- src:36259 | referred to in paragraph (a) bears to the total amount of all
-- src:36260 | other claims (each being a claim the claimant of which is
-- src:36261 | one who, if the claimant had brought an action under
-- src:36262 | section 234, would have been entitled to the amount of
-- src:36263 | compensation specified under section 234(2) or (2A)(a)(i))
-- src:36264 | which have been proved to the court.
@ref s 236(3A) (src:36246-36264)
GIVEN
    `the amount of compensation that the claimant would have been entitled to is specified under section 234(2) or (2A)(a)(i)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the amount of compensation that the claimant would have been entitled to, if the claimant had brought an action under section 234, specified under section 234(2) or (2A)(a)(i)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236(3A) the compensation amount ordered is the lesser of paragraphs (a) and (b)` MEANS
    IF `the amount of compensation that the claimant would have been entitled to is specified under section 234(2) or (2A)(a)(i)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the amount of compensation that a claimant would have been entitled if the claimant had brought an action under section 234 is specified under section 234(2) or (2A)(a)(i)"

@ref s 236(3A) (src:36246-36264)
GIVEN
    `the amount of compensation which the claimant has proven to the satisfaction of the court that the claimant would have been entitled to` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of compensation which the claimant has proven to the satisfaction of the court that the claimant would have been entitled to if the claimant had brought an action under section 234 against the contravening person?
    `the maximum recoverable amount (the answer under section 234(6))` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum recoverable amount under section 234(6)?
    `the total amount of all other claims proved to the court` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total amount of all other claims (each being a claim the claimant of which would have been entitled to compensation specified under section 234(2) or (2A)(a)(i)) which have been proved to the court? (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 236(3A) the compensation amount ordered for the claimant` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the amount of compensation which the claimant has proven to the satisfaction of the court that the claimant would have been entitled to` AT MOST 0
        THEN 0  -- nothing proven, nothing ordered (this also keeps the share below from dividing by zero)
        IF `the amount of compensation which the claimant has proven to the satisfaction of the court that the claimant would have been entitled to` AT MOST (`the maximum recoverable amount (the answer under section 234(6))` TIMES `the amount of compensation which the claimant has proven to the satisfaction of the court that the claimant would have been entitled to` DIVIDED BY (`the amount of compensation which the claimant has proven to the satisfaction of the court that the claimant would have been entitled to` PLUS `the total amount of all other claims proved to the court`))
        THEN `the amount of compensation which the claimant has proven to the satisfaction of the court that the claimant would have been entitled to`
        OTHERWISE `the maximum recoverable amount (the answer under section 234(6))` TIMES `the amount of compensation which the claimant has proven to the satisfaction of the court that the claimant would have been entitled to` DIVIDED BY (`the amount of compensation which the claimant has proven to the satisfaction of the court that the claimant would have been entitled to` PLUS `the total amount of all other claims proved to the court`)  -- FORK F-236-3A: "all other claims" read as all the claims proved, this claimant's own among them (the share is a/(a+others)); the literal ratio a/others is undefined with no other claim
